 "summary_html": "<p>In the book trade, a <b>tipped-in page</b> or <b>tipped-in plate</b> is a page that is printed separately from the main text of the book, but attached to the book. The page may be glued onto a regular page or even bound along with the other pages. There are various reasons for tipped-in-pages, including photographic prints and reviews.</p>",
